    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1164-a4">

                <pb facs="1243" n="1147" xml:id="pg1147"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 4 in No. 207.]</seg></opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Scandella to Mr.
                            Loomis.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Caracas</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1898-07-09"><hi rendition="#italic">July 9,
                        1898</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have been informed by Señor J. C.
                    Mathieu, the minister of foreign affairs, that the Venzuelan Government, in
                    consideration of the treatment to which I was subjected at Ciudad Bolivar on the
                    10th and 11th of May last, when I was arrested and expelled from the country
                    without due process of law, and for no just or adequate reason, is disposed to
                    pay me the sum of $1,600 and reimburse me for all the property of mine which it
                    took or destroyed.</p>
                <p>I am willing to accept these terms, and, if they are at once fulfilled, will ask
                    you, if they meet your approval, to withdraw my claim from the files of the
                    legation.</p>
                <p>Truly, yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">F. Scandella.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Francis B. Loomis</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">United States Minister.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
